Z||000000||Mattyman||11-01-2001||05:24 PM||||I have no idea how to post pics on the forum.  I have PIP but I dont know what to do with it.  I read the stuff about it, but how do u get a post a pic on a board and also in you signature. ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||11-01-2001||06:04 PM||||Assuming you've correctly downloaded PIP, just click on it (while you're on the forum), click Browse, find the pic you're looking for, then click Post.  Once the pic has uploaded, click OK and minimize PIP.  Hit Ctrl-V and your pic should show up in your post (you won't see the pic until you submit the post and return to the thread).<P><BR>If you want a sig line, just click on Profile and scroll down until you see the area for Signature.  Use PIP (the same as you would to upload a pic to a post) to add a pic to your sig.  Just remember to keep the size of the pic small.  (Read Cliffs note at the top left of the screen for more info as to what he wants and doesn't want in a sig.  It's the small link with the flashing arrow.)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||kempo||11-01-2001||09:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mattyman:<BR><B>I have no idea how to post pics on the forum.  I have PIP but I dont know what to do with it.  I read the stuff about it, but how do u get a post a pic on a board and also in you signature. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I never figured it out either <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">, so I just upload the stuff to my own server and link it over, and all is well  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.admist.net/gtsmall.jpg">    <BR>0-60 6.9 seconds||||reg||1
